  &lt;body>
    &lt;p>
&lt;b>The MVF metamodel as per the XMI&amp;#160;specification at&amp;#160;&lt;a href="http://">www.omg.org/spec/MVF/20220501/MVF.xmi&lt;/a>       
&lt;/b>&lt;br>This XMI file, which was imported into this model at &lt;a href="mdel://_19_0_4_c480314_1685901462397_434447_4990" erit:display="NAME" erit:update="AUTOMATIC_UPDATE">MVF ad-22-05-03 XMI&lt;/a>, has missing elements that are present in the PDF spec, see &lt;a href="http://">www.omg.org/spec/MVF/1.0/Beta1/PDF&lt;/a>.

    &lt;/p>

    &lt;p>
The full MVF&amp;#160;metamodel based on the imported &lt;a href="https://www.omg.org/spec/MVF/AboutMVF.rdf">AboutMvf.rdf&lt;/a>&amp;#160;specification is at &lt;a href="mdel://_19_0_4_c480314_1690393176063_646342_14113" erit:display="NAME" erit:update="AUTOMATIC_UPDATE">MVF Metamodel - Per RDF&lt;/a>, which again differs from the XMI&amp;#160;and PDF.&amp;#160;Theoretically these should align.

    &lt;/p>

    &lt;p>
For the resolution stategy see:&amp;#160;&lt;a href="mdel://_19_0_4_c480314_1689859390973_526031_12482" erit:display="NAME" erit:update="AUTOMATIC_UPDATE">MVF Metamodel - Per PDF (no missing elements)&lt;/a>.

    &lt;/p>

